<p>An international aid vessel reached Havana on March 24 carrying solar panels, bicycles, food, and medicine as Cuba faces deepening economic and energy strains. The boat was the first in a flotilla tied to the &quot;Our America Convoy to Cuba,&quot; a campaign involving more than 650 participants from 33 countries who arrived on the island over the weekend with tons of humanitarian supplies. The shipment arrived as recurring shortages of fuel and other goods kept pressuring daily life and the island&#x27;s power system. Several reports described the convoy as an effort by activists to ease the impact of U.S. sanctions and fuel restrictions on Cuba. The broader crisis remains unresolved, but the arrival offered a tangible sign of international solidarity and immediate practical help for communities facing shortages.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/CIq4yi2dc4utyj8gMYFFhWMryqgGAx9_01626pYdE3YY_fXv0rujDaDMtrsM5xtyF-rWgc6vqv7Mldn_wAPzRnhmgrdIu3SnTik8mmJvo5o7ePglH5FpYl86jhm-yvMcNa-VQuLLVPcdzxl_xLxADValp2s3ihmobX0U7APzk1dbBc3S2DpJBAK91ey2mKhGW0HocKhkm4m2pnUd1j4n0q8CsD9o9Z6Ea1NtID5gx-BfNpIsKUwZu79-HIerijvVYW7rwFge39YNtID1Lw' alt='Activists and members of a flotilla coming from Mexico and carrying aid react upon their arrival to Havana’s bay amid a U.S. oil blockade that has dealt a major blow to the island&#x27;s already ailing energy infrastructure, in Havana, Cuba, March 24, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Delayed arrival: The lead boat reached Havana about three days later than planned after running into strong winds, difficult currents, and a battery problem at sea.</li><li>Small-craft mission: The first shipment arrived aboard a shrimp fishing vessel, highlighting that the convoy relied on a modest civilian boat rather than a large aid ship.</li><li>Harbor symbolism: As the boat neared Havana Bay and a colonial-era fortification, activists stood on the cabin roof before docking near the historic waterfront.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Convoy organizers: They described the flotilla as a direct-delivery workaround to ordinary shipping channels, saying sanctions and related restrictions have made it harder to get fuel and other necessities to the island. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/international-convoy-delivers-tons-aid-to-cuba-amid-crisis'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>International activists aboard the flotilla: Using a small civilian fishing boat for the first delivery reinforced the convoy&#x27;s grass-roots, citizen-organized character rather than giving it the feel of a formal state aid mission. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3347810/humanitarian-aid-boat-arrives-cuba-amid-us-blockade-crisis'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-cuba-aid-flotilla-economic-energy-crises/'>Aid vessel arrives in Cuba as economic and energy crises deepen</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/aid-vessel-arrives-in-cubas-as-economic-and-energy-crises-deepen'>Aid vessel arrives in Cuba&#x27;s as economic and energy crises deepen</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3347810/humanitarian-aid-boat-arrives-cuba-amid-us-blockade-crisis'>Humanitarian aid boat arrives in Cuba amid US blockade crisis</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/international-convoy-delivers-tons-aid-to-cuba-amid-crisis'>International convoy delivers tons of aid to Cuba amid crisis</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/aid-vessel-arrives-havana-cubas-economic-energy-crises-131361590'>Aid vessel arrives in Havana as Cuba&#x27;s economic and energy crises deepen</a> - abcnews.com</li></ul>